    {
      "id": "credentials",
      "name": "Credentials",
      "version": "1.5.0-alpha03",
      "url": "https://developer.android.com/jetpack/androidx/releases/credentials#1.5.0-alpha03",
      "detailsHtml": "<p><strong>New Features</strong></p>\n<ul>\n <li>Introduces a new feature, the Restore Credentials. The restore credential is used to restore the user's credential from the previous device to a new Android device. By creating a <code>RestoreCredential</code> for the user, the credential will be automatically transferred over to the user's new device if the user selects the app to be transferred from the old device during the setup stage.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>API Changes</strong></p>\n<ul>\n <li>New classes are added for requesting Restore Credentials.</li>\n <li>A new credential type, <code>RestoreCredential</code>, that can restore credentials in a new device.</li>\n <li><code>CreateRestoreCredentialRequest</code> for creating a new <code>RestoreCredential</code>.</li>\n <li><code>GetRestoreCredentialOption</code> for fetching <code>RestoreCredential</code>.</li>\n <li><code>ClearCredentialStateRequest</code> can be modified to clear the <code>RestoreCredential</code>.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Bug Fixes</strong></p>\n<ul>\n <li>Added a new <code>RestoreCredential</code> API for app-restore purposes (<a href=\"https://android-review.googlesource.com/#/q/If2d40bfded85a64a0e02e005acc1d0790e454b28\">If2d40</a>)</li>\n</ul>",
      "commitsUrl": null
    },
    {
      "id": "fragment",
      "name": "Fragment",
      "version": "1.8.2",
      "url": "https://developer.android.com/jetpack/androidx/releases/fragment#1.8.2",
      "detailsHtml": "<p><strong>Bug Fixes</strong></p>\n<ul>\n <li><code>AndroidFragment</code> now properly handles cases where the parent fragment is put on the Fragment back stack, avoiding 'No view found for id' issues when popping back to that fragment. (<a href=\"https://android-review.googlesource.com/#/q/I94608fed9ada006e5e601ede8adb8be81fae29a0\">I94608</a>)</li>\n <li>Fragments added via the <code>FragmentTransaction.add</code> method that takes a <code>ViewGroup</code> now wait for <code>onContainerAvailable</code> before progressing to <code>onStart()</code>. This affects users of that API, such as <code>AndroidFragment</code>, which now waits for the <code>AndroidFragment</code> to re-enter composition before moving it through <code>onStart()</code>. (<a href=\"https://android-review.googlesource.com/#/q/I94608fed9ada006e5e601ede8adb8be81fae29a0\">I94608</a>)</li>\n</ul>",
      "commitsUrl": "https://android.googlesource.com/platform/frameworks/support/+log/c06fe0a3e7c61f31e0734f93bef3899fae9dc0f4..539527ae77b888b02a3b0ca85afcaea30a416b4e/fragment"
    },
    {
      "id": "games-frame-pacing",
      "name": "Games-Frame-Pacing",
      "version": "2.1.2",
      "url": "https://developer.android.com/jetpack/androidx/releases/games#games-frame-pacing-2.1.2",
      "detailsHtml": "<p><strong>Bug Fixes</strong></p>\n<ul>\n <li>Swappy now uses <code>AChoreographer_postVsyncCallback</code> from API 33 to calculate the presentation time more accurately. This fixes a bug on 120hz devices where frames are dropped.</li>\n</ul>",
      "commitsUrl": "https://android.googlesource.com/platform/frameworks/opt/gamesdk/+log/394f81c696e264c403a8491dd6e37aa89e3da00d..a29e855e6f39df2ba1ef83eb7897c257ee717d66/games-frame-pacing"
    },
